In ancient times, two villages were separated by a barren valley. In the valley lay a Sacred Spring with miraculous powers: any grain cast into its waters would triple before reaching the bottom.

The Spring demanded a ritual between two chosen villagers, one from each side. The first villager, the Giver, would receive five measures of grain. Whatever portion they cast into the Spring would multiply threefold, emerging on the other side for the Receiver. The Receiver could then choose what amount to send back across the valley to the Giver.

